<%# The dollar view of one quota window: what a full one is estimated to be
    worth, how much of it is left, and how much of THAT spot work may touch.

    "$ remaining" is the headline because it is the only figure that answers
    "how much capacity do we have" — a percentage cannot be compared to a
    reserve, a burn rate, or a decision about whether one more session fits.

    Rendered only when the model has dollars for this window. On a deployment
    where the calibration cron has never run there is nothing honest to print,
    and a $0.00 would read as "exhausted" rather than as "not yet estimated" —
    so the line says which it is instead. %>
<% if window.nil? %>
<% elsif window.dollars? %>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-600" id="<%= dom_id %>">
    <strong><%= capacity_money(window.remaining_usd) %> remaining</strong>
    of an estimated <%= capacity_money(window.capacity_usd) %> window ·
    <%= capacity_money(window.reserve_usd) %> reserved for priority
    (<%= window.reserve_pct %>%) ·
    <strong><%= capacity_money(window.remaining_spot_usd) %></strong> left for spot work.
    <span class="text-gray-400">
      Estimated in Opus list price from
      <%= number_to_currency(window.estimate.sample_cost_usd.to_f, precision: 0) %> of spend at
      <%= (window.estimate.sample_utilization.to_f * 100).round(1) %>% utilization,
      <%= time_ago_in_words(window.estimate.computed_at) %> ago.
    </span>
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-gray-400" id="<%= dom_id %>">
    No dollar estimate for this window yet — QuotaCapacityCalibrationJob needs a window with
    measurable spend and utilization before it can price one. The spot gate paces this window on
    percentages until then.
  </p>
<% end %>
